{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source","id":1012357,"title":"Supernaturals are sleepwalkers in 1.0 source?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-04T20:31:38-08:00","id":1012357,"title":"Supernaturals are sleepwalkers in 1.0 source?","content":"Hey all, my storyteller wants to know where in MTA 1.0 it says that supernaturals like changelings and vampires don't trigger disbelief and/or paradox because they are all sleepwalkers. I know I read it somewhere in there, but am having a hard time finding the page again because of the terrible organization of this book.<br /> <br /> Can someone help me out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T21:33:59-08:00","id":1012375,"title":"","content":"Sleepers are explicitly mortal humans and thus the PCs of other supernaturally-empowered gamelines are no more subject to the Sleeping Curse than spirits are \u2014 a Sleepwalker is a mortal that is not a Sleeper, and thus is treated as though they were a mage or other supernaturally-empowered being for the purposes of vulnerability to Quiescence et al.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that changelings and vampires are all Sleepwalkers as it is that Sleepwalkers lack one of the qualities that sets the vast majority of mundane humans apart from the various types of monster that live among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T21:50:35-08:00","id":1012379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1012375#post1012375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepers are explicitly mortal humans and thus the PCs of other supernaturally-empowered gamelines are no more subject to the Sleeping Curse than spirits are \u2014 a Sleepwalker is a mortal that is not a Sleeper, and thus is treated as though they were a mage or other supernaturally-empowered being for the purposes of vulnerability to Quiescence et al.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that changelings and vampires are all Sleepwalkers as it is that Sleepwalkers lack one of the qualities that sets the vast majority of mundane humans apart from the various types of monster that live among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok great, is there anywhere is explicitly states that in any of the 1.0 MTA books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T21:58:39-08:00","id":1012385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gadren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1012379#post1012379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok great, is there anywhere is explicitly states that in any of the 1.0 MTA books?</div> </div> </div> </div>The lexicon on page 20 of the corebook, for one thing. &quot;A mortal who is not Awake&quot; is literally the definition of a Sleeper, and Sleepwalkers are defined as a subset of Sleepers. Likewise, Disbelief is defined as something that happens to Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T00:47:43-08:00","id":1012434,"title":"","content":"On page 274 of the Core 1e:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the powers of supernatural creatures do not trigger Disbelief. Vampires,<br /> werewolves, spirits, ghosts and other strange beings can use<br /> their powers freely before the eyes of Sleepers. Mages theorize<br /> that Disbelief is a Sleeper\u2019s soul denying the truth of the<br /> Supernal World, as displayed by vulgar Awakened magic.<br /> The powers of other creatures, mages believe, originate in<br /> the Fallen World and do not stir the soul\u2019s memory of its<br /> fallen tragedy. In a sense, Disbelief is a near Awakening, but<br /> one that denies Awakening itself. </div> </div> </div>Now, this is probably a bit of word trickery on the part of the author. While they might not invoke -disbelief-, I'm pretty sure they invoke their own disbelief like thing for their powers (at least in the case of Vampires,Werewolves, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:31:27-08:00","id":1012513,"title":"","content":"I've personally always felt that the authors were double dipping on that rule (the one that let's other major splats remember magic). The reason that sleepers cannot remember magic is because of the sleeping curse, which is supposed to be a Supernal Truth (or probably more accurately, an anti-Truth). Becoming a vampire or a changeling, or transforming into a werewolf has absolutely nothing to do with seeing a Supernal Truth, especially since the authors are so adamant about not creating consistent crossover material for the major splats. Ergo, the other supernatural splats should also have to deal with the sleeping curse.<br /> <br /> OR, if you really want them to be immune then experiencing the supernatural often enough and in a decently...intimate? Powerful? Traumatic? way should consistently create sleepwalkers. Granted that trauma is the most likely choice such people will be fairly broken, thus the veil is still protected. In addition, it makes it easy to explain the other splats being able to remember seeing magic since, by definition, they ARE supernatural.<br /> <br /> At least that's my take on it. It's obviously not cannon at all, but I feel like it makes more sense than what the authors have presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:55:21-08:00","id":1012524,"title":"","content":"In Sleepwalker portion of the book, there is literally a merit that mentions that thorough something traumatic, you became a Sleepwalker. It's called Fitful Slumber and requires suffering 3 or more Supernal/Abyssal Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:13:14-08:00","id":1012534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1012524#post1012524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Sleepwalker portion of the book, there is literally a merit that mentions that thorough something traumatic, you became a Sleepwalker. It's called Fitful Slumber and requires suffering 3 or more Supernal/Abyssal Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:18:14-08:00","id":1012538,"title":"","content":"Ooooh right. Sorry! My brain just sparked up I read that paragraph, with a neon sign of &quot;there is something in the book right here&quot;, and by the time I got to confirm it, I forgot what kind of thread it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:22:06-08:00","id":1012540,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough I can't find anything explicit about this, even in the Chicago rulebook that's supposed to deal with crossovers. I'm glad they made it explicit in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:24:53-08:00","id":1012541,"title":"","content":"The Chicago book was, by a quirk if scheduling, written before Mage 1e was finished. You shouldn't take it as an authority on anything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T09:08:30-08:00","id":1012615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1012513#post1012513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've personally always felt that the authors were double dipping on that rule (the one that let's other major splats remember magic). The reason that sleepers cannot remember magic is because of the sleeping curse, which is supposed to be a Supernal Truth (or probably more accurately, an anti-Truth).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sleeping Curse is part of most typical human souls and particularly keys off of the same setting elements that prompt the vast majority of humanity to deliberately ignore the supernatural. The vast majority of supernatural beings do not have typical human souls. A &quot;Supernal Truth&quot; is a metaphysically distant refined form of something that exists in the Phenomenal World in some form, and the Sleeping Curse is a concentrated subset of the broader tendency of the supernatural to prompt mortals to say nothing and drink to forget. There is no contradiction here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Becoming a vampire or a changeling, or transforming into a werewolf has absolutely nothing to do with seeing a Supernal Truth, especially since the authors are so adamant about not creating consistent crossover material for the major splats. </div> </div> </div>The metaphysical quality of &quot;shies away from the supernatural as a defense mechanism against its deleterious effects on mortal minds, particularly in as distilled a form as what mages work with&quot; by simple necessity has to interact with &quot;you have been changed into an inherently supernatural being.&quot; You may as well say that typical saltwater fish ought to drown if put in the waters of the abyssal depths \u2014 &quot;I can't even remotely cope with the day-to-day existence of the supernatural despite breaking about twenty laws of physics when I get up in the evening&quot; doesn't produce a coherent baseline for a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, it makes it easy to explain the other splats being able to remember seeing magic since, by definition, they ARE supernatural. </div> </div> </div>That's literally how it works already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T09:18:35-08:00","id":1012620,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1012434#post1012434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 274 of the Core 1e: Now, this is probably a bit of word trickery on the part of the author. While they might not invoke -disbelief-, I'm pretty sure they invoke their own disbelief like thing for their powers (at least in the case of Vampires,Werewolves, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of that seems to be that other supernatural magic from vampires, werewolves, etc doesn't invoke disbelief. Not necessarily that Vampires and Werewolves don't invoke it when witnessing supernal magic. The best thing I see off-hand is what someone else said, sleepers are described as 'mortals' and a lot of disbelief relates to aspects of the soul. Whereas most supernatural beings have an altered soul in comparison to an ordinary human. Obviously some splats are more extreme than other sin that regard. Whereas I think demons don't have souls and werewolves are half spirits? Not 100% on the details for 1E settings there. But you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T17:14:55-08:00","id":1012879,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help, all. Sleepers = Always Mortals in 1e and Changelings = Not Mortals was satisfactory.<br /> I'm playing a Changeling Lord Sage of the Unknown Reaches, which allows my changeling to take the Imbue Item merit from MtA (among other things), and it'd be kind of a problem if he caused a paradox every time he used his item from the merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T02:19:20-08:00","id":1013075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1012615#post1012615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleeping Curse is part of most typical human souls and particularly keys off of the same setting elements that prompt the vast majority of humanity to deliberately ignore the supernatural. The vast majority of supernatural beings do not have typical human souls. A &quot;Supernal Truth&quot; is a metaphysically distant refined form of something that exists in the Phenomenal World in some form, and the Sleeping Curse is a concentrated subset of the broader tendency of the supernatural to prompt mortals to say nothing and drink to forget. There is no contradiction here.<br /> <br /> The metaphysical quality of &quot;shies away from the supernatural as a defense mechanism against its deleterious effects on mortal minds, particularly in as distilled a form as what mages work with&quot; by simple necessity has to interact with &quot;you have been changed into an inherently supernatural being.&quot; You may as well say that typical saltwater fish ought to drown if put in the waters of the abyssal depths \u2014 &quot;I can't even remotely cope with the day-to-day existence of the supernatural despite breaking about twenty laws of physics when I get up in the evening&quot; doesn't produce a coherent baseline for a game.<br /> <br /> That's literally how it works already.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were true, then those that had been exposed to the supernatural enough to just barely change them (minor splats in all games) would not be subject to the sleeping curse. However Dave has explicitly stated that they do still suffer from the sleeping curse and that the reason for that is that their exposure to the supernatural has nothing to do with the Supernal realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T03:57:40-08:00","id":1013091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1013075#post1013075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that were true, then those that had been exposed to the supernatural enough to just barely change them (minor splats in all games) would not be subject to the sleeping curse. However Dave has explicitly stated that they do still suffer from the sleeping curse and that the reason for that is that their exposure to the supernatural has nothing to do with the Supernal realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're dead wrong. Minor splats don't suffer Quiescence, if they have any supernatural power they count as at least a Sleepwalker. If anything Dave has said the exact opposite of your claim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T05:15:46-08:00","id":1013103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1013075#post1013075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [...] ...those that had been exposed to the supernatural enough to just barely change them (minor splats in all games) would not be subject to the sleeping curse. [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>This IS exactly what happens. Now you might argue about what &quot;exposed enough&quot; or &quot;changed barely&quot; is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T05:40:26-08:00","id":1013105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012357-supernaturals-are-sleepwalkers-in-1-0-source?p=1013103#post1013103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This IS exactly what happens. Now you might argue about what &quot;exposed enough&quot; or &quot;changed barely&quot; is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rules as written, there's really not much ambiguity concerning &quot;exposed enough&quot; or &quot;changed barely.&quot; Either the character possess the Sleepwalker Merit or as described below in the corebook,<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While not always brought into Awakened society, the Fallen<br /> World hides a wide spectrum of human beings who qualify as<br /> Sleepwalkers, though they may never have any run-in with direct<br /> evidence of the Supernal or Abyss. <b>Any character possessing<br /> Integrity and a Supernatural Merit that reflects an internal talent<br /> or inborn ability is immune to the Curse.</b> Having a cursed<br /> camera that shows you when people will die does not make you<br /> a Sleepwalker. Being able to know what a serial killer is thinking<br /> due to a strange ability to get in his head does push back the Curse.<br /> Drinking the blood of a vampire does not make you a Sleepwalker,<br /> but developing mystical powers from that bond would. Being a kin<br /> to shapeshifters and half-spirits would make you a Sleepwalker. </div> </div> </div>Mage 2e, p. 303.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T